<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/817.jpg" alt="A portrait of a holstein cow" width="450" height="450" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Portrait of 817. 12x12, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This is another painting on a medium texture linen. The surface is hard to photograph - a cellphone picture from the side shows the painting better than a head-on shot.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">The cow looks pretty much as she appeared in real life but the setting was too complex to make a good painting so, instead, I</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">&nbsp;used a simple background of viridian, bright red, and cad yellow light. I added some of this color to the figure's mid-tones to help everything relate.</span></p>
